WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.120
Suppose you want a mouse in which one type of neuron glows when its calcium rises.

2
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:11.600
You also want to switch that same type on with light.

3
00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:16.360
Put the gene for green fluorescent protein behind a promoter that every cell reads,

4
00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:18.080
and you get a green mouse.

5
00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:21.440
But you need the tools in one cell type, and nowhere else.

6
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:22.600
How?

7
00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:24.270
Two kinds of tool do the work.

8
00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:28.850
A reporter is an engineered protein that changes its light when a signal happens.

9
00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:33.410
G -Camp is a calcium reporter, built from green fluorescent protein.

10
00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:38.290
An actuator is an engineered protein that changes cell activity on command.

11
00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:41.370
Channel rhodopsin 2 is an actuator.

12
00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:45.890
Blue light opens its pore, cations flow in, the neuron fires.

13
00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.690
G -Camp's blue light opens it too.

14
00:00:49.433 --> 00:00:51.313
Now give each gene a stop.

15
00:00:51.733 --> 00:00:56.073
Put a stop signal in front of the reporter gene, between two sites called LOX -P.

16
00:00:56.533 --> 00:00:58.393
The two sites point the same way.

17
00:00:58.793 --> 00:01:01.813
The actuator gene gets its own stop in the same way.

18
00:01:02.173 --> 00:01:04.733
With the stop in place, neither gene is read.

19
00:01:05.517 --> 00:01:08.177
Kree is an enzyme from a bacterial virus.

20
00:01:08.857 --> 00:01:11.997
It cuts and rejoins DNA at LOX -P sites.

21
00:01:12.637 --> 00:01:16.757
When two sites point the same way, Kree removes what lies between them.

22
00:01:17.417 --> 00:01:18.837
The stop is cut out.

23
00:01:19.457 --> 00:01:23.717
The cut is permanent, so that cell and its descendants can read the gene.

24
00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:29.200
So who makes Cre? Make it from a promoter active mainly in one cell type.

25
00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:32.640
That cell type cuts out the stops, and makes both proteins.

26
00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:35.660
In most other cells the stops stay in place.

27
00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:37.680
Check each line with a reporter.

28
00:01:38.583 --> 00:01:41.143
To build the mouse, breed three parts together.

29
00:01:41.743 --> 00:01:46.143
The first is Kree, placed in a gene that only your neuron type reads.

30
00:01:46.623 --> 00:01:48.883
The second is a reporter behind a stop.

31
00:01:49.383 --> 00:01:51.503
The third is an actuator behind a stop.

32
00:01:52.343 --> 00:01:56.643
Cells that make Kree remove the stops, so mainly they and their descendants make

33
00:01:56.643 --> 00:01:58.663
both proteins. Keep this rule.

34
00:01:59.123 --> 00:02:01.603
Tools wait behind stops, and Kree removes them.

35
00:02:01.983 --> 00:02:03.123
Check the line with a reporter.
